+# Task 2 report — inventory accounting checkpoint complete
+
+Task 2 has an evidence-linked outcome for every requested quarter and a documented daily historical observation boundary. Root alone made all SEC requests. This agent performed local preparation, verification and register updates only. The checkpoint establishes listing availability and accounting; source-body formats, historical ingestion completeness and arbitrary outage recovery remain unverified.
+
+Read the Task 2 brief including Global Constraints, Stage 1 §5.1 and parent §4.2. Applied clean-code to the isolated investigation helper. Production packages, parser/catalog, production tests, infrastructure and protected baseline artifacts remain outside this task's edits.
+
+## Results
+
+The pinned end is 2026Q4. `quarterly.csv` contains exactly 68 unique quarter summaries for 2010Q1–2026Q4, including exactly 48 development units from 2015Q1. All 68 summaries are `available` based on successful retained directory listings containing master representations. Its 304 child representation rows include both current full-index root children and year/QTR children; their relationship remains a Task 3 body comparison, not an equality inference.
+
+The root full-index listing, all 17 requested year directories and all 68 quarter directories were inspected. Observed quarterly alternatives are `master.Z`, `master.gz`, `master.idx`, `master.zip` (69 child rows each including the root), `master.sit` (19) and `master.z` (9). Directory-listed sizes remain explicitly labeled as listing-declared with units unverified; exact listing dates and sizes remain in the retained children metadata.
+
+`daily.csv` has 2,176 rows. The daily root and all 17 year directories from 2010 through 2026 were inspected. The first and last available quarter of every year were inspected; 2026Q3 was also inspected as the preceding quarter and 2026Q4 as current/handoff. Thus 35 quarter listings succeeded and 33 middle quarters are explicitly `listed_uninspected`. All 68 requested quarter boundary units have honest outcomes. No inaccessible/missing directory was called a successful empty listing. Observed daily master entries are IDX (1,902), GZIP extension (185), uppercase Z (1) and ZIP (1). These counts are listing representations, not specimen validation.
+
+The required 2026-10-01 handoff appears explicitly and has actual discovered `master.20261001.idx` in SEC-0139. An already-published `master.20261002.idx` is available in that same listing. No weekend/holiday filename was manufactured.
+
+## Acquisition and shared access accounting
+
+The accepted root-only window was activated 2026-10-05T23:40:28.753726+00:00 with deadline 2026-10-06T00:25:28.753726+00:00. The root inventory command completed 2026-10-05T23:41:43.654694+00:00, exit 0. Attempts SEC-0001–SEC-0139 retained 1,609,165 original entity bytes; every directory response succeeded; zero retries, redirects, specimens or access-denial halts. JSON was sufficient throughout; XML/HTML fallback was prepared and checked offline but was not exercised live.
+
+Root subsequently retrieved official SEC access guidance through the same helper as SEC-0140, exit 0. At independent verification, shared accounting was 140 attempts, 1,689,512 bytes and zero specimens, without a halt. The original deadline/caps remain authoritative; Task 3 must reuse this exact state/ledger/lock. This checkpoint does not reset or extend the window.
+
+The helper retains immutable intent, original entity body, SHA-256, all response headers, UTC receipt, response status, discovered schema/children and selection decision. It enforces TLS verification, identity content encoding, no redirects, 0.34-second sequential starts, absolute deadline, 15-second connection/DNS signal bound and 60-second read ceiling bounded by remaining window; shared 240-attempt/536870912-byte/12-specimen caps; five attempts per URL across the ledger; Retry-After-aware backoff; persistent denial halt; and conservative interrupted-attempt/orphan-byte recovery with no silent replay. A retained socket supports `Connection: close`. Matrices refuse rerun/overwrite. Ledger initiation is appended and the terminal row atomically completed; one row corresponds to one attempt.
+
+## Independent verification and retained commands
+
+- `python3 -m py_compile specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/investigation-tools/sec_inventory.py`: exit 0.
+- `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/investigation-tools/check_inventory_offline.py`: exit 0, retained output and command receipt. Canonical URL/traversal guards, JSON/XML/HTML observed type validation, external/parent HTML rejection, inactive-window refusal, interruption/orphan-byte recovery, mocked Connection:close handling, synthetic 68/48 inventory, explicit handoff and repeat-output refusal passed. Synthetic/mock output is clearly labeled and establishes no live source claims. A local check initially counted the daily root in its expected 68 quarter units; that check was corrected to exclude the root, with no implementation change.
+- `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/investigation-tools/check_inventory_evidence.py`: exit 0. Independently recomputed inclusive counts; verified unique summaries, development boundary, allowed statuses, retained evidence references, every listed representation against actual retained child entries, original byte counts and SHA-256 for all 140 attempts, immutable intent existence, shared attempt/byte accounting and at least 0.34-second start spacing. Confirmed required handoff row and all 68 daily boundary units. Exact result is `inventory-evidence-check.json`, with `inventory-evidence-check-command.json`.
+- Root inventory command/start/end/exit are retained in `inventory-root-command.json`, with complete stdout/stderr. Official documentation retrieval has its own `sec-documentation-root-command.json` and output artifacts.
+
+## Selection and remaining limits
+
+`task-2-specimen-candidates.json` proposes nine actual-child URLs: quarterly ZIP bodies for 2010Q1, 2015Q1, 2015Q4, 2016Q1, 2026Q3 and 2026Q4; root ZIP for the current-root/year-QTR relationship; and daily IDX bodies for 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-02. These cover intended/development boundaries, year transition, latest closed/open quarter, root relationship, handoff and published daily source within the 12-specimen cap. Root makes the actual Task 3 selection. Root clarified that its final matrix will cover daily year and quarter transitions, using actual retained daily entries for 2025-12-31/2026-01-02 and 2026-09-30/2026-10-01, with the handoff role reused. The additional actual-child references are in `task-2-daily-transition-advisory.json`; the earlier proposed quarterly transition specimens are advisory and may be omitted. Only Task 3 selects the final matrix.
