+With explicit root coordination, appended SEC-0001–SEC-0140 evidence, E-T2-COVERAGE, E-T2-DAILY, E-T2-CANDIDATES and E-T2-DOC-BRIDGE to the evidence index; appended D-14 without replacing historical discrepancy rows; and appended Task 2 shared accounting to access-window.md. Preserved original decision/boundary records and original listing bytes. Root may resume register writes after this interval is released.
+
+Self-review: requested accounting and retained-child/hash checks pass; failed/uninspected states stay honest; optional codecs remain unselected; no ingestion/body support claims; no SEC access by this agent; no protected baseline restoration or production edits. Task 2 is ready for root review. Stage 1 readiness and Task 3 body investigation remain incomplete.
+
+
+## Review repair: incomplete chunked responses
+
+Root review identified that the generic exception path dropped `http.client.IncompleteRead.partial`: a failed chunked response could consume entity bytes without retaining/hash-counting them before a retry. Applied systematic-debugging and reproduced before fixing. The direct offline mock returned `prefix` then raised `IncompleteRead(partial)`; the failing check showed only six prefix bytes retained instead of all thirteen bytes. A minimal fix sends the exception's partial bytes through the same original write/hash/state-accounting path, then re-raises so the response remains failed and never increments complete specimens.
+
+Local stdlib source inspection revealed that `_read_chunked` chains the truncated current-chunk exception separately from its outer completed-chunks partial. A second red reproduction used the real `http.client.HTTPResponse` over an in-memory HTTP chunked stream: outer prefix six bytes plus current truncated chunk four bytes. The final fix includes the chained `IncompleteRead` partial payloads before retaining and accounting, then preserves failure. Requested read amount remains bounded by remaining shared bytes. The direct case passed with both a sufficient 64-byte cap and an exact thirteen-byte cap; the real-client truncated-chunk case retained/hash-counted all ten entity bytes, remained failed, and recorded zero completed specimens.
+
+The retained exact command is `python3 specs/evidence/sec-filing-index-ingestion/stage-1/investigation-tools/check_inventory_offline.py`. Both red reproductions exited 1; final full offline checks exited 0. Compilation exited 0. Original red/green stdout/stderr and command receipt are retained as `investigation-tools/incomplete-read-*.stdout.txt`, `incomplete-read-*.stderr.txt` and `incomplete-read-check-command.json`. Previous offline results and actual acquisition originals remain intact. No SEC/network requests or shared-register writes occurred during this repair. Root review must accept the repair before Task 3 access continues.
